@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = replace-with-admin-jwt
@dispatcherToken = replace-with-dispatcher-jwt
@customerToken = replace-with-customer-jwt
@courierToken = replace-with-courier-jwt
@orderId = replace-with-id-from-automatic-flow-create
@manualOrderId = replace-with-id-from-manual-flow-create
@cancelOrderId = replace-with-id-from-cancellation-flow-create
@courierId = replace-with-id-from-operational-courier-list
@currentOrderId = replace-with-id-from-current-assignment

# Start with the README local profile and demo seed. Run individual requests, not the whole file.
# Fill tokens and IDs from responses. Automatic, manual, and cancellation flows use separate new orders.
# After assignment, courierToken must belong to the selected courier. Refresh currentOrderId for each delivery.
# Use tokens returned by this API's login endpoint with the current JWT_ISSUER.
# Invalid issuer/identity claims, signatures, or timestamps return 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED.
# Valid tokens with the wrong endpoint role return 403 ACCESS_DENIED.
# API errors include details: [] except VALIDATION_FAILED, which lists field/message pairs without rejected values.

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs

### Log in as the seeded customer; set customerToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@delivery.local",
  "password": "DemoPass123!"
}

### Log in as the seeded dispatcher; set dispatcherToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dispatcher@delivery.local",
  "password": "DemoPass123!"
}

### Log in as the seeded admin; set adminToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@delivery.local",
  "password": "DemoPass123!"
}

### Log in as a seeded courier; set courierToken
# Use courier.two@delivery.local instead if that courier is selected for the manual flow.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "courier.one@delivery.local",
  "password": "DemoPass123!"
}

### Automatic flow: create a new delivery order; set orderId from the 201 response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pickupAddress": "Istiklal Cd. No:1, Beyoglu",
  "pickupLatitude": 41.036900,
  "pickupLongitude": 28.985000,
  "dropoffAddress": "Bagdat Cd. No:10, Kadikoy",
  "dropoffLatitude": 40.970000,
  "dropoffLongitude": 29.057000
}

### List customer delivery orders with defaults: page 0, size 20
# Response is {items, page, size, totalElements, totalPages}.
# Only the authenticated customer's orders are included, newest first (createdAt DESC, id DESC).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Request the second page of ten customer orders
# page is zero-based (0..21474836); size is optional (1..100).
# An empty or beyond-last page returns 200 with items: [] and matching totals.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=1&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Invalid pagination: 400 VALIDATION_FAILED with page and size details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=-1&size=101
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Get customer delivery order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Get customer delivery order timeline
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Update courier location before automatic assignment
# Allowed during delivery without changing availability. Stale writes return 409 COURIER_UPDATE_CONFLICT.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/location
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "latitude": 41.032000,
  "longitude": 28.978000
}

### Update courier availability
# Idle couriers only. Active deliveries return 409 COURIER_AVAILABILITY_CHANGE_NOT_ALLOWED.
# A stale concurrent write returns 409 COURIER_UPDATE_CONFLICT; reload state before retrying.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "AVAILABLE"
}

### Auto-assign nearest eligible courier
# A concurrent order/courier write can return 409 ORDER_ASSIGNMENT_CONFLICT; inspect current state before retrying.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders/{{orderId}}/auto-assign
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Get the authenticated courier's current assignment
# Use the courier identified in the assignment response. Set currentOrderId to the returned id.
# 200 with an ASSIGNED/PICKED_UP order; 204 with no body when idle. Ownership comes from courierToken.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/current
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Mark assigned courier order as picked up
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/{{currentOrderId}}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Mark picked-up courier order as delivered
# Success sets the courier to AVAILABLE. A concurrent courier/order write may return 409 COURIER_UPDATE_CONFLICT.
# On conflict, completion and its timeline event roll back; reload current state before retrying.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/{{currentOrderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Confirm the courier is idle after completion: 204 with no body
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/current
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Review completed order history: created, assigned, picked up, delivered
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### List operational orders with defaults: all statuses, page 0, size 20
# DISPATCHER or ADMIN only. Response is {items, page, size, totalElements, totalPages}.
# Items include customer/courier details across all customers, ordered by createdAt DESC, id DESC.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Filter operational orders by status and page
# Optional status: PENDING, ASSIGNED, PICKED_UP, DELIVERED, CANCELLED; omitted or empty means all.
# page is zero-based (0..21474836); size is 1..100. Totals count matching orders only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders?status=PENDING&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Request the next matching page
# Empty or beyond-last pages return 200 with items: [] and matching totals.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders?status=PENDING&page=1&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Unknown operational status: 400 INVALID_REQUEST_PARAMETER with details: []
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders?status=UNKNOWN
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Invalid operational page bounds: 400 VALIDATION_FAILED with page and size details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders?page=-1&size=101
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### List operational couriers with defaults: all availability states, page 0, size 20
# DISPATCHER or ADMIN only. Response is {items, page, size, totalElements, totalPages}.
# Only courier users are included, ordered by id ASC; profile/location fields can be null.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/couriers
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Filter operational couriers by availability and page
# Optional availability: AVAILABLE, UNAVAILABLE, ON_DELIVERY; omitted or empty means all.
# page is zero-based (0..21474836); size is 1..100. Totals count matching couriers only.
# AVAILABLE is stored availability, not a guarantee of assignment eligibility.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/couriers?availability=AVAILABLE&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Request the next matching courier page
# Empty or beyond-last pages return 200 with items: [] and matching totals.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/couriers?availability=AVAILABLE&page=1&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Unknown availability: 400 INVALID_REQUEST_PARAMETER with details: []
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/couriers?availability=UNKNOWN
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Invalid courier page bounds: 400 VALIDATION_FAILED with page and size details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/couriers?page=-1&size=101
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Manual flow: create a separate pending order; set manualOrderId from the 201 response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pickupAddress": "Taksim Square, Beyoglu",
  "pickupLatitude": 41.036900,
  "pickupLongitude": 28.985000,
  "dropoffAddress": "Kadikoy Pier",
  "dropoffLatitude": 40.990900,
  "dropoffLongitude": 29.023300
}

### Manually assign an idle, available courier selected from the operational courier list
# Set courierId from a real courier item's id, not an admin/customer id. ADMIN may also use this endpoint.
# Different pending orders cannot claim the same courier concurrently; the losing assignment rolls back.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders/{{manualOrderId}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courierId": {{courierId}}
}

### Discover the manual assignment; set currentOrderId from the response
# Log in as the selected courier and replace courierToken first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/current
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Pick up the manually assigned order
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/{{currentOrderId}}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Complete the manually assigned order
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/orders/{{currentOrderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}

### Review the manually assigned order's completed timeline
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{manualOrderId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Cancellation flow: create another pending order; set cancelOrderId from the 201 response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pickupAddress": "Taksim Square, Beyoglu",
  "pickupLatitude": 41.036900,
  "pickupLongitude": 28.985000,
  "dropoffAddress": "Kadikoy Pier",
  "dropoffLatitude": 40.990900,
  "dropoffLongitude": 29.023300
}

### Cancel only the new, owned PENDING order: 200 with status CANCELLED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Review the cancelled order's timeline: ORDER_CREATED, ORDER_CANCELLED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Optional: register a customer (201; repeated email returns 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass123"
}

### Optional: create a dispatcher user as admin (201; repeated email returns 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dispatcher@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass123",
  "role": "DISPATCHER"
}

### Missing token: 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders

### Wrong role: 403 ACCESS_DENIED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Reassign the completed automatic-flow order: 409 ORDER_ASSIGNMENT_NOT_ALLOWED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dispatch/orders/{{orderId}}/auto-assign
Authorization: Bearer {{dispatcherToken}}

### Invalid order id: 400 INVALID_REQUEST_PARAMETER
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Unknown availability enum: 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/couriers/me/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{courierToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "UNKNOWN"
}

### Invalid fields: 400 VALIDATION_FAILED with email and password details
# Both fields are reported as "must not be blank"; code and message remain unchanged.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

### Invalid managed role: details name the request field "role"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass123",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}

### Intentionally malformed JSON: 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"customer@example.com","password":
